---
import ProseLayout from '../layouts/ProseLayout.astro';
import { site, contact } from '../config/site';
import { withBase } from '../lib/url';

/**
 * DRAFT — needs review by Cronos legal before launch.
 * This is a working GDPR-shaped policy that matches what the site actually
 * does today (one third-party form processor, no analytics, no cookies).
 * If analytics or any other processor is added, this page must be updated.
 */
---

<ProseLayout
  title="Privacy policy"
  eyebrow="Legal"
  description={`How ${site.name} handles personal data submitted through this website.`}
  lastUpdated="21 August 2026"
>
  <div class="mb-10 rounded-[2px] border border-rule bg-accent-wash p-5 text-accent-ink">
    <p class="text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed">
      <strong class="font-semibold">Draft pending legal review.</strong> This
      policy accurately describes what the website currently does, but it has
      not yet been reviewed by {site.parentOrg}&rsquo;s legal team. Replace this
      notice once it has.
    </p>
  </div>

  <p>
    This policy explains what personal data {site.name} collects through{' '}
    {site.domain}, why we collect it, and what rights you have under the EU
    General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR).
  </p>

  <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
  <p>
    {site.name}, part of {site.parentOrg}, is the data controller for personal
    data submitted through this website.
  </p>
  <p>
    {contact.address.street}, {contact.address.postalCode}{' '}
    {contact.address.city}, {contact.address.country}<br />
    <a href={`mailto:${contact.general}`}>{contact.general}</a>
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <p>
    We only collect what you choose to send us. There is no tracking on this
    website.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Form submissions.</strong> The fields you complete on a contact or
      Request for AI form &mdash; typically your name, email address,
      organisation, and the details of your enquiry.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Email correspondence.</strong> Anything you send us directly,
      including any attachments.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Server logs.</strong> Our hosting provider records standard
      technical request data (IP address, timestamp, requested URL, user agent)
      for security and reliability. We do not use these logs to build a profile
      of you.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Why we process it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>To respond to your enquiry.</strong> Legal basis: your consent,
      given when you tick the consent box before submitting a form, and our
      legitimate interest in answering people who contact us.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>To assess a possible working relationship</strong> &mdash; a
      challenge, a startup partnership, a role, a founder conversation, or a
      lab collaboration. Legal basis: steps taken at your request prior to
      entering into a contract.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>To keep the site secure and available.</strong> Legal basis: our
      legitimate interest in operating the website.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We do not sell your data, and we do not use it for automated
    decision-making or profiling.
  </p>

  <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
  <p>
    Form submissions are transmitted by <strong>Web3Forms</strong>, which
    delivers them to our mailbox on our behalf as a data processor. Email is
    handled by {site.parentOrg}&rsquo;s corporate mail infrastructure. Website
    hosting is provided by our hosting partner.
  </p>
  <p>
    Depending on which route you use, your submission may be shared internally
    with the relevant {site.parentOrg} team &mdash; for example, a challenge
    enquiry may involve the practice that works with your sector. We do not
    share it outside the group without your knowledge.
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Enquiries that do not lead anywhere:</strong> deleted within 12
      months.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Talent applications:</strong> retained for 12 months so we can
      contact you about relevant roles, unless you ask us to delete them
      sooner.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Ongoing relationships:</strong> retained for the duration of the
      relationship and for as long as we are legally required to keep the
      records afterwards.
    </li>
    <li><strong>Server logs:</strong> retained for a maximum of 90 days.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>Under the GDPR you have the right to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>access the personal data we hold about you;</li>
    <li>have inaccurate data corrected;</li>
    <li>have your data erased;</li>
    <li>restrict or object to how we process it;</li>
    <li>receive your data in a portable format;</li>
    <li>withdraw consent at any time, without affecting past processing.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    To exercise any of these, email{' '}
    <a href={`mailto:${contact.general}`}>{contact.general}</a>. We respond
    within one month.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you are not satisfied with our response, you can lodge a complaint with
    the Belgian Data Protection Authority (Gegevensbeschermingsautoriteit /
    Autorité de protection des données),{' '}
    <a
      href="https://www.dataprotectionauthority.be"
      target="_blank"
      rel="noopener noreferrer">dataprotectionauthority.be</a
    >.
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    This website sets no cookies and runs no analytics. See our{' '}
    <a href={withBase('/cookies')}>cookie policy</a> for detail.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    We update this policy when what we do changes. The date at the top of the
    page always reflects the current version.
  </p>
</ProseLayout>
